    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm looking at a contract for a shipment of electronic components coming from South Korea to Germany. It says CIF. can you explain exactly what the seller is responsible for under CIF Incoterms 2020?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure! Under CIF Incoterms 2020, the seller is responsible for the costs, risks, and obligations of bringing the goods to the port of shipment in the country of export (South Korea in this case), including export duties and export taxes. The seller must also obtain a contract for carriage, but the buyer assumes responsibility for the cost and risk of the goods from the arrival port (in your case, upon arrival in Germany), including loading the goods onto the vessel, insurance against loss or damage during transit from the port of shipment, and import duties, customs, and other charges.",
